1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Last time on Zombieland Saga, after screwing up our first paid job, we got not one, but two more chances to shine.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
First, we starred in a commercial for Drive-In Toddy and worked our tail feathers off to try and cluck up some quick butts.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The next step in our quest for press was competing in the Gat-Olympics.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
But instead of getting a taste of fame, we just got a mouthful of mud.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Chicken and mud, those must be the ingredients for success!

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
People are bound to know who we are now!

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Uh, why is no one agreeing with me?

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Come on, please tell me we'll make it!

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Ah, damn it! This is starting to get really frustrating.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
How's it possible that none of these girls have social media?

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
And their website's nothing but photos of their past events?

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
I kinda like that. It means they don't just follow the trends.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I know you wanted us to track these kids, but there's nothing to track.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
After a month, you'd think we'd have something to show for it.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
I wonder, who the heck are they?

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
That's what they are saying.

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
I wonder, who the heck are they?

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
I wonder, who the heck are they?

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,500
I wonder, who the heck are they?

20
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,000
Who the heck are they?

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,500
I wonder, who the heck are they?

22
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,000
Hey, time out!

23
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Uh...

24
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
We're still too slow on that last part.

25
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
I'm so sorry.

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
It's okay.

27
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,000
I'll just slow down.

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Hmmm...

29
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,480
This new song has a duet that highlights Ai and Junko.

30
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,260
You two will be front and center.

31
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:30,460
I feel so guilty.

32
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:34,520
I'm supposed to be on lead vocals, but...

33
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,820
Well, it is fast.

34
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,640
We'll just have to focus on perfecting the most crucial parts of the song.

35
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,960
Okay, I'm gonna run through the whole thing myself to see how it flows.

36
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,500
You guys can take a break.

37
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:06,900
Something about her.

38
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:56,252
Hello?

39
00:03:56,252 --> 00:04:04,852
We're out of shampoo.

40
00:04:04,852 --> 00:04:06,952
What's this glowing box?

41
00:04:06,952 --> 00:04:07,952
It's called a computer.

42
00:04:07,952 --> 00:04:13,292
We're going to use it to figure out what kind of idols are big right now.

43
00:04:13,292 --> 00:04:15,292
They come up with the wildest things.

44
00:04:15,292 --> 00:04:16,292
Hey, stop!

45
00:04:16,292 --> 00:04:18,292
You're going to break it.

46
00:04:18,292 --> 00:04:19,292
Oh dear.

47
00:04:19,292 --> 00:04:20,292
My apologies.

48
00:04:20,292 --> 00:04:21,292
Hold on, you guys.

49
00:04:21,292 --> 00:04:24,292
What if Kotoro catches us?

50
00:04:24,292 --> 00:04:25,292
Don't worry.

51
00:04:25,292 --> 00:04:28,292
His nighttime bath should take at least another 20 minutes.

52
00:04:28,292 --> 00:04:29,292
Are you sure?

53
00:04:29,292 --> 00:04:32,292
Yeah, it's my third time doing this.

54
00:04:32,292 --> 00:04:36,952
Hey Ai, do you think Fran Shushu has its own homepage?

55
00:04:36,952 --> 00:04:39,292
I do, and I am not going back to it.

56
00:04:39,292 --> 00:04:41,212
But why not?

57
00:04:41,212 --> 00:04:42,292
You'll die from cringing.

58
00:04:42,292 --> 00:04:43,292
Huh?

59
00:04:43,292 --> 00:04:45,292
Uh, die again, I mean.

60
00:04:45,292 --> 00:04:47,632
Hello?

61
00:04:47,632 --> 00:04:48,632
Uh...

62
00:04:48,632 --> 00:04:49,632
Uh...

63
00:04:49,632 --> 00:04:50,632
Uh...

64
00:04:50,632 --> 00:04:55,972
Anyway, I've been doing a lot of digging around lately.

65
00:04:55,972 --> 00:04:59,972
So much has changed since my day, especially for idols.

66
00:04:59,972 --> 00:05:04,972
Lots of popular groups who seem like they would stay together forever already broke up.

67
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:07,312
Public interest in idols does fluctuate.

68
00:05:07,312 --> 00:05:09,312
Wait, what's that mean for us though?

69
00:05:09,312 --> 00:05:13,312
Even if idols aren't in right now, we'll still try our best.

70
00:05:13,312 --> 00:05:14,312
Okay?

71
00:05:14,312 --> 00:05:16,312
Um, yeah, okay.

72
00:05:16,312 --> 00:05:17,312
Alright.

73
00:05:17,312 --> 00:05:19,312
Who's doing events?

74
00:05:19,312 --> 00:05:20,312
Let me see.

75
00:05:20,312 --> 00:05:24,312
This new technology is so useful.

76
00:05:24,312 --> 00:05:26,312
Just look at them all.

77
00:05:26,312 --> 00:05:27,312
Cool.

78
00:05:27,312 --> 00:05:29,652
Let's start with the ones that seem interesting.

79
00:05:29,652 --> 00:05:31,652
Oh, what's Saga Rock?

80
00:05:31,652 --> 00:05:33,152
That sounds like fun.

81
00:05:33,152 --> 00:05:34,652
Sure does.

82
00:05:34,652 --> 00:05:35,652
Do you like rock?

83
00:05:35,652 --> 00:05:36,652
Yep.

84
00:05:36,652 --> 00:05:39,152
We all know Mentai Rock is huge in Kyushu.

85
00:05:39,152 --> 00:05:40,152
Mentai what?

86
00:05:40,152 --> 00:05:41,152
Haha!

87
00:05:41,152 --> 00:05:42,152
I'll kill you.

88
00:05:42,152 --> 00:05:44,152
But I seriously don't know.

89
00:05:44,152 --> 00:05:49,152
It says here it's the largest outdoor rock event on the island of Kyushu.

90
00:05:49,152 --> 00:05:50,152
No way!

91
00:05:50,152 --> 00:05:52,152
We gotta get in on that!

92
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:56,152
Looks like it'd be easy to get on one of the big stages, but…

93
00:05:56,152 --> 00:06:00,612
It must be amazing to perform at a place like that with so many people!

94
00:06:00,612 --> 00:06:04,312
I've done a lot of press appearances, so I won't even be that nervous!

95
00:06:04,312 --> 00:06:05,912
Yeah, let's go for it!

96
00:06:05,912 --> 00:06:08,652
If we put in enough practice, we'll bring the house down!

97
00:06:08,652 --> 00:06:10,492
It's not that easy though.

98
00:06:10,492 --> 00:06:11,492
Huh?

99
00:06:11,492 --> 00:06:13,152
You have no idea.

100
00:06:13,152 --> 00:06:14,992
The venue's huge.

101
00:06:14,992 --> 00:06:18,152
A lot of work goes into performing somewhere like that.

102
00:06:18,152 --> 00:06:20,312
Oh, right.

103
00:06:20,312 --> 00:06:25,472
It would be better for us to take small steps than dive headfirst into the deep end.

104
00:06:25,472 --> 00:06:26,652
Sorry.

105
00:06:26,652 --> 00:06:28,472
I understand you.

106
00:06:28,472 --> 00:06:32,352
But we don't really have the time to gradually build our popularity.

107
00:06:32,352 --> 00:06:35,472
We need to find a way to get our name out there quick.

108
00:06:35,472 --> 00:06:37,472
Take the group I was in before this.

109
00:06:37,472 --> 00:06:42,472
We played for audiences in the tens of thousands after just a year on the scene.

110
00:06:42,472 --> 00:06:43,972
One year?

111
00:06:43,972 --> 00:06:46,472
How did you attract so many people?

112
00:06:46,472 --> 00:06:51,632
If you're trying to be perfect from the beginning, then you'll never get anywhere.

113
00:06:51,632 --> 00:06:55,632
Fans like to see you improve over time and feel like they're a part of it.

114
00:06:55,632 --> 00:06:56,632
Like it's a journey.

115
00:06:56,632 --> 00:06:57,632
I don't know…

116
00:06:57,632 --> 00:07:02,632
And obviously, we still need to try our best every step of the way.

117
00:07:02,632 --> 00:07:06,792
It's the first time to be perfect.

118
00:07:06,792 --> 00:07:07,792
Hey look!

119
00:07:07,792 --> 00:07:09,792
Isn't that your old group I?

120
00:07:09,792 --> 00:07:10,792
Which one?

121
00:07:10,792 --> 00:07:11,792
Right there!

122
00:07:11,792 --> 00:07:12,792
You see?

123
00:07:12,792 --> 00:07:14,792
They'll be at Sokka Rock!

124
00:07:14,792 --> 00:07:15,792
Iron frill?

125
00:07:15,792 --> 00:07:16,792
Sweet!

126
00:07:16,792 --> 00:07:35,952
Oh, good day to you!

127
00:07:35,952 --> 00:07:40,952
Dear friend!

128
00:07:40,952 --> 00:07:43,112
Shushu!

129
00:07:43,112 --> 00:07:51,112
I have come to bring you good tidings!

130
00:07:51,112 --> 00:07:53,112
I am the great-

131
00:07:53,112 --> 00:07:55,112
That's enough!

132
00:07:55,112 --> 00:07:57,112
Just spit it out!

133
00:07:57,112 --> 00:07:58,112
All right.

134
00:07:58,112 --> 00:08:02,112
I'm delighted to say that I've got some excellent news for you all.

135
00:08:02,112 --> 00:08:05,112
Does anybody want to guess?

136
00:08:05,112 --> 00:08:09,272
You have some fans now!

137
00:08:09,272 --> 00:08:13,712
Thanks to the chicken ad, followed by the Gatalympics coverage, you've gained a bit

138
00:08:13,712 --> 00:08:16,272
of traction online.

139
00:08:16,272 --> 00:08:17,272
Wow!

140
00:08:17,272 --> 00:08:18,272
Really?

141
00:08:18,272 --> 00:08:19,272
What'd I say?

142
00:08:19,272 --> 00:08:21,272
Can't get any better than Drive-In Toddy!

143
00:08:21,272 --> 00:08:25,272
No matter how stupid we look, I guess there's no such thing as bad press.

144
00:08:25,272 --> 00:08:27,272
What are you talking about?

145
00:08:27,272 --> 00:08:32,272
Even when you're covered in mud, Franz Shushu always finds a way to sparkle!

146
00:08:32,272 --> 00:08:35,432
Drive-In Toddy!

147
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:36,432
Huh?

148
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:37,432
You're close!

149
00:08:37,432 --> 00:08:39,432
Let me show you how!

150
00:08:39,432 --> 00:08:40,432
It's like this!

151
00:08:40,432 --> 00:08:41,432
To-ring!

152
00:08:41,432 --> 00:08:42,432
Oh, okay!

153
00:08:42,432 --> 00:08:44,432
I think I get it now!

154
00:08:44,432 --> 00:08:45,432
To-ring!

155
00:08:45,432 --> 00:08:47,432
That's not really it either!

156
00:08:47,432 --> 00:08:48,432
To-ring!

157
00:08:48,432 --> 00:08:49,432
Right!

158
00:08:49,432 --> 00:08:50,432
One more!

159
00:08:50,432 --> 00:08:51,432
To-ring!

160
00:08:51,432 --> 00:08:52,432
Are you even watching-

161
00:08:52,432 --> 00:08:54,432
Who the hell cares?!

162
00:08:54,432 --> 00:08:58,112
Why would I need to master your stupid dance routine?!

163
00:08:58,112 --> 00:09:00,432
Don't you look down your nose at me, Pinocchio!

164
00:09:00,432 --> 00:09:02,592
I own you, remember?!

165
00:09:02,592 --> 00:09:03,592
What, Pinocchio?!

166
00:09:03,592 --> 00:09:05,592
You're not a real boy yet!

167
00:09:05,592 --> 00:09:10,192
Now that I've made that crystal clear, here's your new mission.

168
00:09:10,192 --> 00:09:13,592
You're all about to spend a little quality time with the fans of Franz Shushu.

169
00:09:13,592 --> 00:09:15,592
Short notice, as always.

170
00:09:15,592 --> 00:09:17,592
I already announced it on our homepage.

171
00:09:17,592 --> 00:09:20,752
When you say quality time...

172
00:09:20,752 --> 00:09:23,752
For now, I think we'll start with a photo op!

173
00:09:23,752 --> 00:09:24,752
Wait a minute.

174
00:09:24,752 --> 00:09:26,752
What is he talking about?

175
00:09:26,752 --> 00:09:31,752
Oh, I guess what he means is, the fans will take pictures of us, but not with film.

176
00:09:31,752 --> 00:09:33,752
They'll probably just be digital.

177
00:09:33,752 --> 00:09:34,752
Digital?

178
00:09:34,752 --> 00:09:36,752
Uh, how do I explain?

179
00:09:36,752 --> 00:09:39,352
You don't have to wait for the pictures.

180
00:09:39,352 --> 00:09:41,512
Oh, like a Polaroid, right?

181
00:09:41,512 --> 00:09:42,512
Mmm...

182
00:09:42,512 --> 00:09:46,512
I see, we're taking glamour shots with Polaroids!

183
00:09:46,512 --> 00:09:47,512
Mmm...

184
00:09:47,512 --> 00:09:50,192
No, it's not gonna be a big formal thing.

185
00:09:50,192 --> 00:09:51,512
Actually, it will be.

186
00:09:51,512 --> 00:09:53,512
Whoa, for real?!

187
00:09:53,512 --> 00:09:57,512
Usually there's a mini-concert and some merch sales, then pics.

188
00:09:57,512 --> 00:10:00,512
Merch sales, huh?

189
00:10:00,512 --> 00:10:04,512
We have some t-shirts, but no one wants to wear those tacky things.

190
00:10:04,512 --> 00:10:05,512
You must be confused.

191
00:10:05,512 --> 00:10:08,512
Are you keeping up?

192
00:10:08,512 --> 00:10:09,512
I'm fine.

193
00:10:09,512 --> 00:10:12,512
I've found that getting confused doesn't help much.

194
00:10:12,512 --> 00:10:15,512
I'll just relax and take things as they come.

195
00:10:15,512 --> 00:10:18,512
And after this, I've got an even bigger pan on the fire!

196
00:10:18,512 --> 00:10:22,512
So don't let me down, or you might get cut!

197
00:10:22,512 --> 00:10:35,512
That's it, and we are...

198
00:10:35,512 --> 00:10:37,512
From Choo Choo!

199
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:39,512
Thanks for all your support!

200
00:10:39,512 --> 00:10:40,512
Yeah!

201
00:10:40,512 --> 00:10:41,512
Good morning!

202
00:10:41,512 --> 00:10:42,512
Good morning!

203
00:10:42,512 --> 00:10:43,512
Good morning!

204
00:10:43,512 --> 00:10:44,512
Good morning!

205
00:10:44,512 --> 00:10:45,512
Good morning!

206
00:10:45,512 --> 00:10:46,512
Good morning!

207
00:10:46,512 --> 00:10:48,512
People really showed up!

208
00:10:48,512 --> 00:10:51,512
I can't believe we actually have fans now!

209
00:10:51,512 --> 00:10:56,512
And, uh, if you want, we're gonna have a photo op right after this!

210
00:10:56,512 --> 00:10:57,512
Aw, man.

211
00:10:57,512 --> 00:10:58,512
That's crazy!

212
00:10:58,512 --> 00:11:00,512
You all came here to see us!

213
00:11:00,512 --> 00:11:01,512
I mean...

214
00:11:01,512 --> 00:11:03,512
You guys rock!

215
00:11:07,512 --> 00:11:08,512
It's Coco, dammit!

216
00:11:09,512 --> 00:11:12,512
Ohhhh...

217
00:11:12,512 --> 00:11:14,512
It looks so good!

218
00:11:14,512 --> 00:11:15,512
Ahhhh...

219
00:11:15,512 --> 00:11:18,512
It looks so gross!

220
00:11:18,512 --> 00:11:19,512
Uhhhh...

221
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:20,512
She's warm!

222
00:11:20,512 --> 00:11:22,512
They're warm!

223
00:11:25,512 --> 00:11:27,512
We have the official Fraun Machu-choo T-shirts available…

224
00:11:27,512 --> 00:11:29,512
...as well as these cute hand towels!

225
00:11:29,512 --> 00:11:31,112
these cute hand towels.

226
00:11:31,112 --> 00:11:32,952
Anyone who buys at least one item

227
00:11:32,952 --> 00:11:34,952
will be eligible for the photo session.

228
00:11:36,092 --> 00:11:38,752
When did we have time to get this stuff made?

229
00:11:38,752 --> 00:11:40,992
Yeah, and what's with that weird design?

230
00:11:42,132 --> 00:11:43,392
All right, everyone, it's time

231
00:11:43,392 --> 00:11:45,572
to get those photo sessions rolling.

232
00:11:45,572 --> 00:11:48,792
We'll start with the lines for number zero and number one,

233
00:11:48,792 --> 00:11:51,292
then we'll get number two and number three.

234
00:11:51,292 --> 00:11:52,472
Photo sessions?

235
00:11:52,472 --> 00:11:53,312
With who?

236
00:11:54,572 --> 00:11:57,272
The fans are lined up to take individual photos with us.

237
00:11:57,272 --> 00:11:58,732
What else would this be?

238
00:11:58,732 --> 00:11:59,572
Huh?

239
00:12:04,572 --> 00:12:05,412
Ready!

240
00:12:11,712 --> 00:12:13,652
Here we go, smile!

241
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:18,952
What was that?

242
00:12:18,952 --> 00:12:23,192
Okay, next we'll do photographs for numbers four, five, and six.

243
00:12:23,192 --> 00:12:25,052
Number four, it's your turn.

244
00:12:25,052 --> 00:12:26,192
We'll be using this folding screen.

245
00:12:26,192 --> 00:12:27,332
I can't.

246
00:12:27,332 --> 00:12:28,332
Huh?

247
00:12:28,332 --> 00:12:30,132
I'm not posing for pictures.

248
00:12:30,132 --> 00:12:31,772
But why not?

249
00:12:31,772 --> 00:12:33,512
Hurry up, they're waiting.

250
00:12:33,512 --> 00:12:34,012
No!

251
00:12:35,832 --> 00:12:37,712
But you've got the longest line.

252
00:12:37,712 --> 00:12:39,072
You have to.

253
00:12:39,072 --> 00:12:42,072
Idols are supposed to dazzle people from up on stage.

254
00:12:42,072 --> 00:12:44,252
How does this have anything to do with that?

255
00:12:44,252 --> 00:12:46,212
What's wrong?

256
00:12:46,212 --> 00:12:49,052
What the hell was that?

257
00:12:49,052 --> 00:12:49,932
I'm so disappointed in you.

258
00:12:49,932 --> 00:12:50,932
What's wrong?

259
00:12:50,932 --> 00:12:53,792
Oh.

260
00:12:53,792 --> 00:12:56,472
What the hell was that?

261
00:12:56,472 --> 00:12:58,032
I'm so disappointed in you.

262
00:12:58,032 --> 00:13:00,692
Do you want to know how disappointed I am?

263
00:13:00,692 --> 00:13:05,132
Well, if I had to give you a metaphor, it's like...

264
00:13:05,132 --> 00:13:08,892
Stop zombies!

265
00:13:09,572 --> 00:13:09,912
God!

266
00:13:14,652 --> 00:13:18,252
You do understand that this whole thing was your fault, right, Junko?

267
00:13:18,792 --> 00:13:21,212
Walking out on a job doesn't affect just you.

268
00:13:21,532 --> 00:13:22,792
It hurts all of us.

269
00:13:22,992 --> 00:13:24,672
So that's part of our job?

270
00:13:25,112 --> 00:13:25,852
Of course.

271
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:27,752
But it's so personal.

272
00:13:28,272 --> 00:13:29,732
I don't want to do that.

273
00:13:29,932 --> 00:13:30,712
Listen to me.

274
00:13:31,192 --> 00:13:32,252
Idols do this.

275
00:13:32,512 --> 00:13:34,292
We have fans and they love us.

276
00:13:34,292 --> 00:13:36,652
So they need to feel like we're within reach.

277
00:13:36,952 --> 00:13:38,272
But that's just it.

278
00:13:38,712 --> 00:13:41,552
Besides, you bragged about going big after your first year.

279
00:13:41,992 --> 00:13:43,092
Just from fan events?

280
00:13:43,392 --> 00:13:45,772
Is that more important than being a great performer?

281
00:13:46,192 --> 00:13:46,932
Wait a sec.

282
00:13:47,292 --> 00:13:48,732
Don't put words in my mouth.

283
00:13:48,972 --> 00:13:50,012
You better back off.

284
00:13:50,052 --> 00:13:51,452
Guys, take a chill pill.

285
00:13:51,672 --> 00:13:52,332
She's right.

286
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:53,092
Relax.

287
00:13:53,652 --> 00:13:56,992
I just think we need to decide what our relationship with fans should be.

288
00:13:57,432 --> 00:13:59,512
You're the only one here who doesn't get it.

289
00:13:59,592 --> 00:14:00,832
Oh my god, what do I do?

290
00:14:01,112 --> 00:14:03,112
I agree that we need our fans.

291
00:14:03,112 --> 00:14:06,252
But we have different opinions about the role they should play.

292
00:14:06,732 --> 00:14:09,312
A good performer doesn't have to depend on them.

293
00:14:09,472 --> 00:14:09,832
No.

294
00:14:10,432 --> 00:14:12,992
But being above your fans is so less century.

295
00:14:13,212 --> 00:14:15,492
You aren't exactly fresh blood yourself.

296
00:14:17,072 --> 00:14:18,052
Don't fight!

297
00:14:18,052 --> 00:14:28,012
If you want to be in a real idol group, then you're going to have to leave your fear behind.

298
00:14:28,012 --> 00:14:37,012
That was uncalled for.

299
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:40,572
Hey!

300
00:14:43,572 --> 00:14:44,252
Damn it.

301
00:14:44,252 --> 00:14:49,272
That's employment.

302
00:14:56,952 --> 00:14:57,872
Come on!

303
00:14:57,872 --> 00:15:19,552
I'm not going to be history yet.

304
00:15:19,552 --> 00:15:28,292
Come on, Ai.

305
00:15:28,492 --> 00:15:30,292
Can't you two bury the hatchet already?

306
00:15:30,592 --> 00:15:33,032
Just shake hands and admit you were both wrong.

307
00:15:33,392 --> 00:15:34,892
Yeah, that's a good idea.

308
00:15:35,572 --> 00:15:39,412
I'm sorry, you guys, but I don't feel like I should go back on anything I said.

309
00:15:39,712 --> 00:15:43,792
Just because each side has a valid point doesn't mean the disagreement can't be resolved.

310
00:15:44,472 --> 00:15:47,392
I thought the rest of you were serious about becoming idols.

311
00:15:47,392 --> 00:15:50,292
We just want you and Junko to stay friends.

312
00:15:50,352 --> 00:15:51,532
But we're not friends.

313
00:15:51,712 --> 00:15:52,732
We work together.

314
00:15:53,412 --> 00:15:54,892
You were in show business, Lily.

315
00:15:54,992 --> 00:15:56,372
You should understand that.

316
00:15:56,812 --> 00:15:58,672
Jeez, you don't have to make her cry.

317
00:16:00,692 --> 00:16:02,572
Don't you walk away from me!

318
00:16:03,112 --> 00:16:04,092
I wouldn't worry.

319
00:16:04,912 --> 00:16:06,472
Things will settle down soon.

320
00:16:07,092 --> 00:16:08,272
Won't they, leader?

321
00:16:10,772 --> 00:16:12,492
What a freaking pain!

322
00:16:17,392 --> 00:16:21,392
Come on, hurry!

323
00:16:21,812 --> 00:16:24,572
I told you, I didn't bring a swimsuit.

324
00:16:40,572 --> 00:16:41,352
I'll get it!

325
00:16:41,352 --> 00:16:43,372
Oh, it's you!

326
00:16:45,772 --> 00:16:53,312
I see.

327
00:16:53,932 --> 00:16:56,452
So you're from a generation earlier than me, huh?

328
00:16:56,732 --> 00:16:57,992
It's more like two.

329
00:16:58,552 --> 00:17:00,572
I would have been an old lady by now.

330
00:17:01,252 --> 00:17:06,092
I was just thinking, I've never really had the chance to ask you what kind of idol you used to be.

331
00:17:06,092 --> 00:17:12,052
Back in those days, it just wasn't the norm for idols to have that kind of fan interaction.

332
00:17:12,912 --> 00:17:15,672
Maybe a meet and greet once in a while, but that's all.

333
00:17:16,392 --> 00:17:22,612
So, no matter where we were, on the stage or the tube, there was always a clear boundary.

334
00:17:23,052 --> 00:17:23,272
Hmm?

335
00:17:23,892 --> 00:17:25,632
Um, wait, what about a tube?

336
00:17:26,212 --> 00:17:26,952
I'm lost.

337
00:17:27,432 --> 00:17:30,552
It's an idol's job to give people something to aspire to.

338
00:17:30,552 --> 00:17:34,392
I could never let the fans get close enough to see my flaws.

339
00:17:34,952 --> 00:17:38,552
Or at least, that's the way it was for the idols I knew.

340
00:17:40,532 --> 00:17:45,712
Just like I'd grown up admiring them, I wanted to become a role model for others, too.

341
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:49,472
That's why I worked hard, day in and day out.

342
00:17:49,472 --> 00:17:53,432
I was starting to feel like I'd accomplished that.

343
00:17:54,092 --> 00:17:57,472
And I thought maybe, I could keep on doing it.

344
00:17:58,472 --> 00:18:03,472
But on my way to Saga for my first touring Kyushu...

345
00:18:04,192 --> 00:18:08,792
Hmm.

346
00:18:09,472 --> 00:18:10,872
And that was that.

347
00:18:11,552 --> 00:18:12,412
Oh, Junko.

348
00:18:13,252 --> 00:18:15,492
Not just anyone can be an idol.

349
00:18:16,152 --> 00:18:17,952
The same goes for being a zombie.

350
00:18:17,952 --> 00:18:22,952
And if my approach is holding the team back...

351
00:18:22,952 --> 00:18:27,332
I'm sorry, but I can't be in Franshushu.

352
00:18:27,712 --> 00:18:29,372
I just don't belong.

353
00:18:29,372 --> 00:18:29,792
Hmm.

354
00:18:29,792 --> 00:18:42,792
I...

355
00:18:42,792 --> 00:18:56,472
Found you.

356
00:18:56,472 --> 00:18:58,652
Tell me what's wrong.

357
00:18:59,532 --> 00:19:00,052
Hey!

358
00:19:06,232 --> 00:19:07,912
Well, this is messed up.

359
00:19:09,192 --> 00:19:10,912
You look like a wet cat.

360
00:19:11,252 --> 00:19:12,212
Guess we both do.

361
00:19:13,072 --> 00:19:18,392
You know, if I'm being honest, I don't get all this stuff about being idols and having fans.

362
00:19:18,392 --> 00:19:21,632
But I do know you need guts and good backup.

363
00:19:21,992 --> 00:19:22,892
That's all we've got.

364
00:19:26,292 --> 00:19:27,372
I'm surprised.

365
00:19:27,652 --> 00:19:29,052
You're really scared of lightning?

366
00:19:29,772 --> 00:19:32,312
That's because it's how I died.

367
00:19:32,312 --> 00:19:47,672
Damn, what a way to go.

368
00:19:47,672 --> 00:20:03,512
Talk about legendary.

369
00:20:03,512 --> 00:20:06,552
That's not the kind of legend I want to be.

370
00:20:07,652 --> 00:20:09,412
My story isn't over.

371
00:20:10,072 --> 00:20:11,172
I'm still here.

372
00:20:11,352 --> 00:20:12,692
I'm not history yet.

373
00:20:13,312 --> 00:20:14,852
I don't care if I'm a zombie.

374
00:20:15,472 --> 00:20:17,372
I'm gonna get back on stage again.

375
00:20:17,992 --> 00:20:18,912
And then I'll...

376
00:20:18,912 --> 00:20:23,532
You've always been a firecracker, huh?

377
00:20:38,532 --> 00:20:39,252
Saki.

378
00:20:39,972 --> 00:20:41,132
You're still awake?

379
00:20:41,972 --> 00:20:43,652
Yeah, I had trouble sleeping.

380
00:20:44,432 --> 00:20:45,232
Those two.

381
00:20:45,792 --> 00:20:48,732
If this was my old gang, I'd beat both their asses.

382
00:20:48,992 --> 00:20:49,932
Or maybe worse.

383
00:20:50,492 --> 00:20:51,752
Please don't hurt them.

384
00:20:52,372 --> 00:20:53,272
I won't.

385
00:20:54,112 --> 00:20:57,492
But for real, we won't get anywhere if they keep that up.

386
00:20:57,992 --> 00:20:59,232
They need a wake-up call.

387
00:20:59,872 --> 00:21:01,712
The sooner we can fix this, the better.

388
00:21:03,392 --> 00:21:03,832
Yeah.

389
00:21:09,472 --> 00:21:11,912
Good morning, ladies!

390
00:21:11,912 --> 00:21:12,152
Please?

391
00:21:13,472 --> 00:21:14,072
Look!

392
00:21:14,712 --> 00:21:17,292
I've got great news, so pay attention, please!

393
00:21:17,792 --> 00:21:19,972
Anybody want to guess what?

394
00:21:20,432 --> 00:21:21,572
Fine, I'll tell you!

395
00:21:21,612 --> 00:21:24,252
We're on the newcomer's roster for this year's Saga Rock!

396
00:21:27,592 --> 00:21:29,852
Yes, you may applaud me.

397
00:21:29,972 --> 00:21:31,172
The Saga Rock?

398
00:21:31,572 --> 00:21:32,812
You're kidding me.

399
00:21:32,932 --> 00:21:35,392
This is a once-in-an-after-lifetime chance!

400
00:21:35,772 --> 00:21:37,252
And that means...

401
00:21:37,252 --> 00:21:38,672
You girls better not screw it up.

402
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:42,132
For one day, Saga will be the center of the music world,

403
00:21:42,292 --> 00:21:44,332
and you need to stand at the center of Saga!

404
00:21:44,672 --> 00:21:47,092
This is Franz Shushu's first outdoor show!

405
00:21:47,232 --> 00:21:50,932
Your music will light up the sky and shake the earth!

406
00:21:51,792 --> 00:21:52,292
Thank you!

407
00:21:52,392 --> 00:21:52,772
And we'll see you on the next one!

408
00:21:56,772 --> 00:21:57,252
Bye!

409
00:21:57,652 --> 00:21:58,492
Bye!

410
00:22:01,052 --> 00:22:01,532
Bye!

411
00:22:06,252 --> 00:22:07,492
Bye!

412
00:22:07,532 --> 00:22:07,772
Bye!

413
00:22:08,192 --> 00:22:08,892
Bye!

414
00:22:09,112 --> 00:22:09,212
Bye!

415
00:22:09,312 --> 00:22:09,792
Bye!

416
00:22:12,492 --> 00:22:12,972
Bye!

417
00:22:13,692 --> 00:22:14,112
Bye!

418
00:22:14,552 --> 00:22:14,872
Bye!

419
00:22:15,412 --> 00:22:15,832
Bye!

420
00:22:16,192 --> 00:22:16,732
Bye!

421
00:22:16,932 --> 00:22:17,552
Bye!

422
00:22:17,552 --> 00:22:17,632
Bye!

423
00:22:17,752 --> 00:22:18,632
Bye!

424
00:22:18,732 --> 00:22:18,992
Bye!

425
00:22:19,072 --> 00:22:19,852
Bye!

426
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:31,987
Junko here. If I'm gonna be in everybody's way, I might as well turn into a big stupid mushroom.

427
00:23:31,987 --> 00:23:38,987
Next time on Zombieland Saga, Episode 7. But it's Zombie Mental Saga. I'll go away now.

